[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: SDD004 Consensus assumption: the Raft log is a single ordered history and Raft is not re-proved
UID: DOC-SDD004
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text
  VIEW_STYLE: Narrative

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: grammar.sgra

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD004
TITLE: Consensus assumption: the Raft log is a single ordered history and Raft is not re-proved
STATEMENT: >>>
The local group shall use Ra as the Raft log. The design shall treat a committed Ra index as the single ordered history and shall not include a proof of Raft. Commands shall be submitted only by the current Ra leader. Acceptance is a three-member Ra cluster in one Erlang node that commits one clearance and rejects a command from a follower that is not the leader.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Re-proving Raft is out of scope. Using a known library keeps the assumption explicit.
<<<
DAL: A
REQUIREMENT_LEVEL: Low-Level
VERIFICATION: Test
ASSUMPTIONS: Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SRS004
- TYPE: File
  PATH: apps/atc_tower/src/atc_ra_machine.erl
